From a1687744a338b3170a20041d8f0cb29f3a226042 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Qianhui Xu <xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:38:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] phy: qcom: mipi-csi2: add SM8750 2.4.0 lane settings

SM8750 carries the 2.4.0 generation of the CSIPHY, wired in two-phase
mode.  Its register map is the one the vendor driver describes as
csiphy_2ph_v2_4_0_reg: 103 entries over four data lanes at a 0x400 stride
and a clock lane at 0xe00, with the same address, mask and parameter type
as lane_regs_x1e80100 (the 2.1.2 generation) and only the data byte of 13
entries changed:

  - 0x0000/0x0400/0x0800/0x0c00, the per-lane 0x0000 register, is 0x8c
    instead of 0x8e,
  - 0x0008/0x0408/0x0808/0x0c08/0x0e08, the settle count register, is
    0x19 instead of 0x10,
  - 0x0060/0x0460/0x0860/0x0c60, the skew calibration register, is 0xfd
    instead of 0xbd.

Of those, only the first group is written as a constant by this driver:
the settle count entries are overwritten with the value computed from the
link frequency, and the skew calibration entries are skipped until the
driver learns to apply the DT skew flag.  The table keeps the vendor
values for all 13 entries anyway so that it stays a faithful copy.

Add lane_regs_sm8750[] with those values, together with the 2ph power-up
writes this driver's init path relies on and which the vendor table keeps
in a separate sequence, and describe the 3nm SM8750 block as its own
configuration.  The 3nm block puts its common status window at
0x1000 + 0x138 rather than at 0x1000 + 0xb0; that window is only read to
print the hardware version, so this change leaves the offset alone instead
of carrying a second copy of the per-SoC status offset rework that the
3nm part support in flight is adding.

Signed-off-by: Qianhui Xu <xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
